[#:seon.task{:name "no-repl-entrance-creates-a-task"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "No REPL entrance creates a task. Detectors, errors, users and agents can add a task only by hand-editing resources/seon/tasks EDN, the bootstrap exception of spec 7.14. `seon.task/create!` (spec 7.8) must submit a declaration, with the basis it read, to the one task writer: the handle is seon.id over [ns name kind], a duplicate or a supplied handle that differs from its aspect refuses, and a competing revision returns base, current and proposed (7.16). Today every task in this directory was written by hand."
             :must-read #{seon.task/index-tasks! seon.task/task-basis seon.task/task-handle seon.task/tasks-tx}
             :evidence #{"docs/prds/agent-platform/landing/lane-impl-task-slice2-2026-09-25.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/task-log-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/language-requirements-2026-09-24.md"}}
#:seon.task{:name "open-tasks-with-all-proofs-green-are-not-flagged"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Every bucket-D task in tmp/orchestrator/triage.tsv whose proofs were checked on 2026-10-07 has all proofs green while the task stays open: seon.call-preparation/acquired-functions-get-no-supplied-defaults (2 proofs), seon.fn/host-bound-class-list-copies-interpreter-config, seon.sci.eval/program-change-check-scans-the-whole-history, seon.render/a-renderer-is-chosen-by-key-presence (2 proofs), seon.db/the-query-wrapper-costs-36x-datahike and seon.repl/reply-map-is-not-edn-when-elided-or-rendered (`my.test/check` on branch agent ctx-ex-1 and recorded results on default). Either the work is done and the task should close, or the proof does not test the intent (e.g. seon.db/the-query-wrapper-costs-36x-datahike's intent is a 36x cost, its proof bounds armed work). A green proof on an open task must be visible in the task's view and in the queue, and a task's proof must fail before its fix."
             :must-read #{seon.task/task-edges seon.test/recorded-result}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/context-examples/README.md"}}
#:seon.task{:name "tasks-have-no-done-when-and-name-subjects-only-through-must-read"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.task/task-edges` answers :subjects #{} for most tasks: the functions a task is about are on the task's `:seon.task/must-read`, not on the functions' :seon/tasks. Context assembly from the proc transcript (S4) must union both. No :seon.task/done-when exists; under the 2026-10-07 ruling done = the proofs green, so a task without proofs cannot be launched: refuse assignment of a task with no proof test."
             :must-read #{seon.task/task-edges seon.task/assign!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/context-examples/README.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "task-text-references-are-never-resolved",
            :kind :function,
            :intent
            "Over the 392 tasks installed on default: `:seon.task/must-read` names 41 symbols that resolve to no function, test or namespace (e.g. seon.print.value/bounded-text, seon.cluster/mcp-get-value, my.program/overrides); intents name 44 qualified symbols, 42 qualified keywords and about 34 namespaces that resolve to nothing (e.g. :seon.issue/id, :seon.task/done-when, my.plan). `seon.task/task-findings` checks only :seon/tasks tags. A task brief built from references shows a dangling reference as a hole. Done when task ingestion reports dangling must-read symbols per task (the program gate refusing new ones) and intent references are resolved by the same reference index, with counts in the notes.",
            :must-read #{seon.task/task-findings},
            :evidence
            #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/context-design/reference-kinds-notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-runtime-created-task-is-never-written-back"
  :kind :function
  :intent "A task made by `seon.task/create!` exists only in the database: a deftest tagged :seon/tasks with its ns/name is refused at publication as a dangling id, and a reset loses it. Lanes hand-copied 8+ tasks into resources/seon/tasks on 2026-10-08. CLAUDE.md: \"Files are the write-back of accepted entities.\" Correct: the task's home write-back stages the accepted task into resources/seon/tasks/<ns>.edn like any accepted entity, and ingesting that file entry over the runtime row yields one task (see a-file-task-is-refused-while-a-runtime-task-holds-its-symbol). Proof: create! then write-back produces the EDN entry, and a deftest tagged with the new task publishes without a dangling-id refusal."
  :must-read #{seon.task/create! seon.task/index-tasks!}
  :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/split/reconciled-plan.md"}}]
